  <title>Global voice settings</title>
  <p>
    Use Global Voice Settings preferences for speech settings that always apply, regardless of
    which voice type Orca is using. Examples include the speech system and synthesizer,
    capitalization style, punctuation level, how numbers and colors are spoken, whether the
    pronunciation dictionary is used, and language switching. To choose the voices Orca uses,
    use Voice Sets preferences. The Global voice set holds the voices Orca normally uses; Global
    Voice Settings controls behavior that applies regardless of the voice set or voice type.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-global-voice-settings">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Speech</gui> category, <gui>Global Voice Settings</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Global Voice Settings</gui>
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Speech system:</gui> Selects the speech
              system Orca uses. Supported systems include Speech Dispatcher and Spiel.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Speech synthesizer:</gui> Selects the speech
              synthesizer. Examples include espeak-ng and Voxin.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Punctuation Level</gui>: Controls how much
              punctuation Orca speaks. Choices: None, Some, Most, All.
            </p>
            <list>
              <item>
                <p>
                  <gui>None</gui>: Requests that
                  punctuation symbols not be spoken.
                </p>
              </item>
              <item>
                <p>
                  <gui>Some</gui>: Requests that some
                  punctuation symbols be spoken. The speech system determines which symbols are
                  included.
                </p>
              </item>
              <item>
                <p>
                  <gui>Most (default)</gui>: Requests that most
                  punctuation symbols be spoken. The speech system determines which symbols are
                  included.
                </p>
              </item>
              <item>
                <p>
                  <gui>All</gui>: Requests that all
                  punctuation symbols be spoken.
                </p>
              </item>
            </list>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Capitalization style</gui>: Controls how Orca
              indicates uppercase letters. Choices: Voice only, Icon, Spell. Default: Voice
              only.
            </p>
            <list>
              <item>
                <p>
                  <gui>Voice only</gui>: Uses the
                  configured uppercase voice without adding another indication.
                </p>
              </item>
              <item>
                <p>
                  <gui>Icon</gui>: Uses the configured
                  uppercase voice and plays a tone before speaking an uppercase letter.
                </p>
              </item>
              <item>
                <p>
                  <gui>Spell</gui>: Uses the configured
                  uppercase voice and says capital before speaking an uppercase letter.
                </p>
              </item>
            </list>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Speak numbers as digits</gui>: When enabled, Orca
              speaks 123 as 1 2 3. When disabled, Orca sends the number to the synthesizer,
              which likely speaks it as one hundred and twenty three. Default: off.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Speak colors as names</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks colors by name, such as light blue, instead of as RGB values. Default:
              on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Insert pauses to break up speech</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca inserts brief pauses between parts of a spoken presentation, such as name,
              role, state, mnemonic, and tutorial message. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Use pronunciation dictionary</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca uses pronunciation dictionary entries. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Language Switching</gui>: Controls when Orca
          switches voices based on language.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Document content</gui>: Automatically
              switch voice based on document content language. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>UI elements</gui>: Automatically
              switch voice based on UI element language. Default: off.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Limit switching to configured voices</gui>: Only switch
              languages that have a configured voice set. Default: off.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
